#
#  ERA5 (CDS reanalysis, ECMWF table-128 GRIB1) for the Rust met_intermediate
#  writer, with the "ecmwf" map source.  GRIB1 only.  Names, units and soil
#  layers follow WPS's Vtable.ECMWF; the parameter set is what
#  `woof fetch --source era5` retrieves (woof/fetch.py ERA5_REQUIRED_*).
#
#  * Soil layers are keyed twice: native CDS level type 112 with the layer bounds
#    in centimetres (100-255 is how GRIB1 spells the 100-289 cm layer), and the
#    CDO-flattened level type 1 the packaged Vtable.ERA5_CDO uses.  The first
#    row carrying a name supplies its units and description.
#  * HGT is derived from GEOPT / 9.81, 2 m RH from 2 m dewpoint, SOILHGT from
#    the surface geopotential, SNOW from snow depth in metres of water
#    equivalent and SNOWH from SNOW (rrpr.F); their rows only name the output.
#  * A combined retrieval carries every analysis time in one file, so the door
#    runs met_intermediate with --select-valid-time: one valid time per file.
